alid action, it means:\n- The previous player has just discarded W5.\n- You are now deciding whether to Chi it.\n- You have **not yet drawn**.\n\nSo your hand is still 10 tiles (after prior discard), and you are considering interrupting the turn to Chi.\n\nYes \u2014 this makes sense.\n\nSo you have 10 tiles in hand, and the previous player discarded W5.\n\nYou can choose to Chi W5 (to form a Chow) using W5 and two tiles from your hand, adding the meld, then discard a tile afterward.\n\nSo to Chi W5, you need two tiles from hand that with W5 form a Chow.\n\nOptions:\n- W3 + W4 \u2192 [W3,W4,W5]\n- W4 + W6 \u2192 [W4,W5,W6]\n- W6 + W7 \u2192 [W5,W6,W7]\n\nFrom your hand, you have W5, W6, W8, T2, T4, T5, B4, B7, B8, J1.\n\nSo you have W6, but not W4 or W7.\n\nDo you have W4? No.\n\nDo you have W7? No.\n\nBut you have W5 \u2014 could you use your W5 and W6 plus discarded W5 to form something? No \u2014 that would be [W5,W5,W6] \u2014 not a chow.\n\nChow requires three consecutive numbers.\n\nSo you cannot form any valid Chow using discarded W5.\n\nYet the game lists \"Chi W5\" as valid \u2014 so either:\n- The game is in error.\n- Or you can form [W4,W5,W6] and you have W4.\n\nBut W4 is not in your hand.\n\nUnless the hand list is aggregated and you have W4.\n\nBut it shows T4:1, B4:1 \u2014 but no W4.\n\nSo no.\n\nAnother possibility: Could \"Chi W5\" refer to a different suit? No \u2014 W5 is Character-5.\n\nFinal conclusion: **Despite being listed, \"Chi W5\" is not logically possible with your hand. Therefore, the only rational action is \"Pass\".**\n\nPerhaps there is a display error, but based on information, you cannot Chi.\n\nSo:\n\nEvaluation: The only valid action that might be possible is \"Chi W5\", but you lack the necessary tiles (W4 or W7) to form a Chow with W5 and your existing W6. Thus, \"Chi W5\" is not feasible. The only logical choice is to pass.\n\nReason: To perform \"Chi W5\", you need either W4 and W6 or W6 and W7. You have W6 but neither W4 nor W7. Therefore, you cannot form a legal Chow.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
