ll, no peng on W8, so likely safe.\n\nSimilarly, F4: previous player discarded F4, so they don\u2019t need it.\n\nBoth are safe.\n\nBut **W8** contributes less to potential chows.\n\nFinal decision: **Discard W8**\n\nReason: It is the most isolated tile with the least potential to form useful chows or melds. W5 and W6 can form a sequence with W7, B7 and B8 can form [B7,B8,B9], while W8 lacks adjacent tiles in hand. F4 and J1 are honor tiles that could contribute to scoring patterns, even if minor. W8 is safer to discard than B1/B3/B4/F4/J1 which are more dangerous or useful.\n\nAnswer: Play W8"}
